I stopped this run without changing anything: issue #28 now needs a decision from Jody, so I added the `needs-decision` label and left a comment on it.

**Why it can't go on:** #28 was waiting only on #30, the setup for the kernel pilot (the `kernel-looper` app, the GitLab project, the access pool and the signing key). #30 is now closed, but as superseded, not done. Jody closed it on 2026-11-06 because #83 replaced it: every looper now gets its GitHub tokens from the tacplus-looper and tacplus-manager Apps. That setup will never be built, so #28's acceptance can't be met: one real kernel issue end to end, with a PR by `kernel-looper[bot]`. There is no other open issue it could wait on instead. Closing it unfinished, and deciding what happens to its code and its line in ROADMAP.md, are not my calls.

**What I asked Jody to choose** (my recommendation first):
- **(a)** Close #28 as superseded. Remove the pilot's code, which was merged in 5b4d031 but never deployed, through one cleanup follow-up issue, and drop line 29 of ROADMAP.md.
- **(b)** Close #28 as superseded, but keep the code as a starting point for a later setup where the model holds no write credential.
- **(c)** Rescope #28 so that split (the model holds no write credential) runs on the #83 Apps instead. That is new design work and would need its own decision and acceptance criteria.

No gates ran, because there was nothing to verify.
